title: Councils of the unemployed
subtitle: Those without work have no factory to organise in.
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/arbeiterbew.jpg
frequency: 150
tags: kpd_mass
view-if: mass_unemployed_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; mass_unemployed_timer = 3

= Councils of the unemployed

The unemployed are outside the factories and the unions. They are queueing at the labour exchanges and standing in the corridors of the welfare offices. If we don't organise them, no one will, except, perhaps, the Right.

- @councils: Form councils of the unemployed in every district.
- @march: Organise a hunger march to the Landtag.
- @root: Not this month.
- @easy_discard

@councils
subtitle: No cost.
on-arrival: unemployed_kpd += 5*campaign_mult
go-to: root

The councils meet at the labour exchanges. They do small, concrete things: they accompany people to the welfare office, they prevent evictions and they organise soup. They bind the unemployed to the party, and they also bind the party to the unemployed, which is harder to manage.

@march
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; unemployed_kpd += 4*campaign_mult; pro_republic -= 1; y23_strikes += 0
go-to: root

Thousands march behind the red banners to the seat of the Landtag. The police block them, and the press describes the march as a disturbance of the peace. The unemployed know why they came, and no member of the Landtag who heard them can claim they did not.
